      "sourceText": "1. 把 `std::atomic` 理解成“一定 lock-free”。\n2. 把 `volatile` 当作线程同步工具。\n3. 用多个 atomic 表达一个必须整体一致的状态，却没有额外同步。\n4. 在不理解内存模型时随意把所有操作改成 `memory_order_relaxed`。\n5. 自己实现自旋锁并在临界区长时间工作，导致 CPU 空转。\n6. 认为“atomic 变量安全”就等于“包含它的整个类都线程安全”。",
      "translatedText": "1. Treat `std::atomic` as \"must be lock-free\"\\.\n2. Treat `volatile` as a thread synchronization tool\\.\n3. Use multiple atomics to represent a state that must be consistent as a whole, without additional synchronization\\.\n4. When not understanding the memory model, arbitrarily change all operations to `memory_order_relaxed`\\.\n5. Implement a spinlock yourself and work for a long time in the critical section, causing the CPU to spin idle\\.\n6. Believe that \"atomic variables are safe\" means \"the entire class containing them is thread\\-safe\"\\.",
      "provider": "deepseek",
      "model": "deepseek-flash",
      "usage": {
        "inputTokens": 220,
        "outputTokens": 115,
        "costUsd": 0.000204
